@startuml initiator_withdrawal_diagram_without_states
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title Initiator Withdrawal Sequence Diagram (Without States)
box "User Side" #AliceBlue
actor User #LightCyan
participant Iso #LightBlue
participant Boomlet #LightPink
participant ST #Violet
participant Niso #LightGreen
end box
participant WT order 99 #Red
actor Peers order 100
participant SAR order 101 #Yellow

autonumber "<b>[00]"
|||
note over User, SAR:  **Notation** \n withdrawal follows Setup and the state at the end of setup is inherited for all entities except Iso which loses state on shutdown. \n "_i" in variable name indicates an integer less than 5, identifying peers, any operation done on this kind of variable is done on each element of a vector containing every peers' version of that value. \n Boomlet's niso_0_event_block_height is updated with freshly received value in each message containing it. \n Each message is represented by a name composed of stage||sender||receiver||# in which # represents the #th message from sender to receiver in that stage. \n In the withdrawal diagram peer_0 represents the peer that initiates the transaction and peer_1 represents one of the non-initiator peers. \n Each entity inside user-side box of each peer_i is represented by entityName_i. \n Some steps between initiator and non-initiator run asynchronously and concurrently, these steps when associated with non-initiator are denoted by an 'n' character at the end of step#.
group Transaction Initiation
note over User, SAR
<b>PARAMETERS
# #define DURESS_CHECK_INTERVAL_IN_BLOCKS
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_NON_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TO_RECEIVING_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_ALL_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVALS_BY_INITIATOR_PEER
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_SAR_RESPONSE_BY_WT
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_INITIATOR_AND_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TO_RECEIVING_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_ALL_PEERS
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PING_TO_RECEIVING_ALL_PINGS_BY_WT_AND_HAVING_SAR_RESPONSE_BACK_TO_WT
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PONG_BY_WT_TO_REVIEWING_THE_PONG_IN_PEERS_BOOMLET
# #define TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PING_BY_OTHER_PEERS_TO_REVIEWING_THE_PING_IN_PEER_BOOMLET
# #define JUMP_IN_BLOCKS_IF_LAST_SEEN_BLOCK_LAGS_BEHIND_NISO_EVENT_BLOCK_HEIGHT_IN_BOOMLET
# #define REQUIRED_MINIMUM_DISTANCE_IN_BLOCKS_BETWEEN_INITIATOR_PEER_TX_APPROVAL_AND_RECEIVING_ALL_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVALS_BY_INITIATOR_PEER
# #define REQUIRED_MINIMUM_DISTANCE_IN_BLOCKS_BETWEEN_PEER_TX_COMMITMENT_AND_RECEIVING_ALL_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_PEERS
# #define REQUIRED_MINIMUM_DISTANCE_IN_BLOCKS_BETWEEN_PING_AND_PONG
end note
rnote over User: User generates PSBT using a otherwise independent watch-only wallet module.

' Step 1
User o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalNisoInput1 \n psbt
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives psbt from User. Niso checks that most_work_bitcoin_block_height has passed milestone_block_0 from boomerang_descriptor, \n derives tx_id from psbt and stores it. Niso also checks to see if psbt inputs are satisfiable. It sends the psbt alongside the latest \n block_height to Boomlet.
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  most_work_bitcoin_block_height := rpc_client.get_block_height()
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert most_work_bitcoin_block_height >= boomerang_params.boomerang_descriptor.milestone_block_0 .
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  tx_id := psbt.derive_tx_id(). \n niso_0_event_block_height := most_work_bitcoin_block_height
hnote over Niso #Pink: Assert hydrate_psbt(psbt) != Null

' Step 2
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage1 \n psbt \n niso_0_event_block_height
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {psbt, niso_0_event_block_height} from Niso and checks to see if the niso_0_event_block_height has passed \n milestone_block_0. Boomlet then derives tx_id from psbt, creates st_preview_nonce, uses st_preview_nonce for ST freshness, encrypts it for st_0_identity_pubkey and sends the envelope to Niso.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert niso_0_event_block_height >= boomerang_params.boomerang_descriptor.milestone_block_0 .
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  tx_id := psbt.derive_tx_id() \n st_preview_nonce := random_bytes(32)
group ST_check(tx_id)
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  tx_id_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{ \n content: {tx_id}, \n nonce: st_preview_nonce \n} \n tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_review"), content: tx_id_with_nonce)

' Step 3
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage1 \n tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Boomlet and forwards it to ST.

' Step 4
Niso o-> ST:  <b>WithdrawalNisoStMessage1 \n tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Niso, decrypts it, separates the nonce and sends the tx_id to User.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  tx_id_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_review"), envelope: tx_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st) \n tx_id := tx_id_with_nonce.content.tx_id \n st_preview_nonce := tx_id_with_nonce.nonce

' Step 5
ST o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalStOutput1 \n tx_id
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives tx_id from ST and checks to see if it matches that of the psbt he generated. User then informs ST of his acknowledgement of tx_id.
hnote over User #Pink: Assert tx_id == psbt.derive_tx_id()

' Step 6
User o-> ST:  <b>WithdrawalStInput1 \n magic: "withdrawal_initiator_peer_approved_that_txid_received_is_the_same_as_the_one_derived_from_withdrawal_psbt"
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives {magic: "withdrawal_initiator_peer_approved_that_txid_received_is_the_same_as_the_one_derived_from_withdrawal_psbt"} from User. \n ST then signs the tx_id_with_nonce it received with st_privkey and encrypts it with boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. It then sends this encrypted \n message to Niso.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st := sign_message(st_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_review_approval", tx_id_with_nonce) \n tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_review_approval"), content: tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st)

' Step 7
ST o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalStNisoMessage1 \n tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from ST and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 8
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage2 \n tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Niso, decrypts it, verifies st_0_identity_pubkey's signature \n and checks if the content is the same as the one sent i.e. User has acknowledged the tx_id and the message is fresh. Boomlet then creates initiator_approval_nonce and computes withdrawal_id. It then generates \n peer_0_tx_approval containing withdrawal_id, initiator_approval_nonce, and event_block_height, signs it with boomlet_0_identity_privkey and encrypts it for wt. It \n then encrypts psbt for every other boomlet_i using withdrawal_id-bound envelopes. Boomlet sends withdrawal_id, the resulting psbt_encrypted_collection, \n and peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt to Niso.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_review_approval"), envelope: tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(st_0_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_review_approval", tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert tx_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st.content == tx_id_with_nonce
end group
end group
group Transaction Approval
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  initiator_approval_nonce := random_bytes(32) \n withdrawal_id := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/withdrawal_id", canonical_encode(setup_instance_id, tx_id, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, initiator_approval_nonce))
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  peer_0_tx_approval := TxApproval{\n withdrawal_id: withdrawal_id,\n approval_nonce: initiator_approval_nonce,\n event_block_height: niso_0_event_block_height \n} \n peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", peer_0_tx_approval)\n _peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", wt_pubkey, "wt", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: wt_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_approval", withdrawal_id), content: peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0) \n psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_i_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_psbt", withdrawal_id), content: psbt) [1 <= i <= 4] \n psbt_encrypted_collection := Collection<psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]

' Step 9
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage2 \n withdrawal_id \n peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt \n psbt_encrypted_collection: Collection<psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {withdrawal_id, peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt, psbt_encrypted_collection: Collection<psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]} \n from Boomlet and forwards them to WT.

' Step 10
Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage1 \n <b>[start of non-initiator diagram] \n withdrawal_id \n peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt \n psbt_encrypted_collection: Collection<psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives {withdrawal_id, peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt, psbt_encrypted_collection: Collection<psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]} \n from Niso. WT decrypts peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt using canonical context {"withdrawal_tx_approval", withdrawal_id}, verifies boomlet_0_identity_pubkey's signature, \n checks that the signed peer_0_tx_approval carries the same withdrawal_id, and checks that the event_block_height is fresh. \n Then it constructs its own wt_tx_approval containing withdrawal_id and most_work_bitcoin_block_height and signs it. \n It sends to each non-initiator peer wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt, peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0 and psbt encrypted by that peer's boomlet_identity_pubkey.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  most_work_bitcoin_block_height := rpc_client.get_block_height()
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0 := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: channel_keys(wt_privkey, "wt", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: wt_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_approval", withdrawal_id), envelope: peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt)
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0) == True
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_0_tx_approval := peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0.content
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert peer_0_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id
hnote over WT #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height >= (most_work_bitcoin_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT) \n Assert peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height <= most_work_bitcoin_block_height .
hnote over WT #Lavender:  _wt_tx_approval := WtTxApproval{\n withdrawal_id: withdrawal_id,\n event_block_height: most_work_bitcoin_block_height}\n wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt := sign_message(wt_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/wt_tx_approval", _wt_tx_approval)

' Step 11
WT o-> Peers:  <b>WithdrawalWtNonInitiatorNisoMessage1 \n wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt \n peer_0_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_0 \n psbt_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomlet_i
autonumber 24 "<b>[00]"

' Step 24
Peers o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNonInitiatorNisoWtMessage1 \n withdrawal_id \n peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT collects one valid peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i from every active setup peer, sorts the valid approvals into ordered_peer_tx_approvals in active setup peer order, \n and derives ordered_non_initiator_peer_tx_approvals := ordered_peer_tx_approvals[1..4]. Each receiver verifies this WT-supplied ordering before computing approved_withdrawal_id.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: channel_keys(wt_privkey, "wt", peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: wt_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_approval", withdrawal_id), envelope: peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt) [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_i_tx_approval := peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert peer_i_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert peer_i_tx_approval.event_block_height >= max((most_work_bitcoin_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_NON_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT), wt_tx_approval.event_block_height) [1 <= i <= 4] \n Assert peer_i_tx_approval.event_block_height <= most_work_bitcoin_block_height [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Lavender:  ordered_peer_tx_approvals := Collection<peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i> [0 <= i <= 4] sorted in active setup peer order by peer_ids_collection \n ordered_non_initiator_peer_tx_approvals := ordered_peer_tx_approvals[1..4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert count(ordered_peer_tx_approvals) == count(peer_ids_collection) \n Assert ordered_peer_tx_approvals contains exactly one approval per active setup peer \n Assert ordered_peer_tx_approvals has no missing peers and no duplicate signers \n Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", ordered_peer_tx_approvals[i]) == True [0 <= i <= 4]

' Step 25
WT o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage1 \n ordered_peer_tx_approvals \n wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt

' Step 26
WT o-> Peers:  <b>WithdrawalWtNonInitiatorNisoMessage2\n ordered_non_initiator_peer_tx_approvals

' Notes associated with Step 25
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {ordered_peer_tx_approvals, wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt} from WT. Niso verifies each \n boomlet_i_identity_pubkey's signature on each peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i and verifies wt_pubkey's signature on wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt. \n It checks withdrawal_id to match what was sent, the event_block_heights to be in the appropriate range, and ordered_peer_tx_approvals to contain exactly one approval per active setup peer in peer_ids_collection order. \n It computes approved_withdrawal_id from withdrawal_id and ordered_peer_tx_approvals for local tracking, then forwards ordered_peer_tx_approvals with the latest block to Boomlet.
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  most_work_bitcoin_block_height := rpc_client.get_block_height()
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(wt_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/wt_tx_approval", wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt) == True
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  _peer_i_tx_approval := peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [0 <= i <= 4] \n _wt_tx_approval := wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt.content \n niso_0_event_block_height := most_work_bitcoin_block_height
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert _peer_i_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id. [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert _wt_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id.
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", ordered_peer_tx_approvals[i]) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  approved_withdrawal_id := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/approved_withdrawal_id", canonical_encode(withdrawal_id, ordered_peer_tx_approvals))
hnote over Niso #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert wt_tx_approval.event_block_height >= peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height \n Assert wt_tx_approval.event_block_height <= min (peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height + TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT, most_work_bitcoin_block_height)
hnote over Niso #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert peer_i_tx_approval.event_block_height >= max(wt_tx_approval.event_block_height, (most_work_bitcoin_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TO_RECEIVING_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER)) [1 <= i <= 4] \n Assert  peer_i_tx_approval.event_block_height <= (most_work_bitcoin_block_height - REQUIRED_MINIMUM_DISTANCE_IN_BLOCKS_BETWEEN_INITIATOR_PEER_TX_APPROVAL_AND_RECEIVING_ALL_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVALS_BY_INITIATOR_PEER)  [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height >= max((wt_tx_approval.event_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_TX_APPROVAL_BY_WT) , (most_work_bitcoin_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_APPROVAL_BY_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_ALL_NON_INITIATOR_TX_APPROVALS_BY_INITIATOR_PEER)) \n Assert  peer_0_tx_approval.event_block_height <= wt_tx_approval.event_block_height

' Step 27
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage3 \n ordered_peer_tx_approvals \n wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt \n niso_0_event_block_height
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {ordered_peer_tx_approvals, wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt, niso_0_event_block_height} \n from Niso. Boomlet verifies each boomlet_i_identity_pubkey's signature on each peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i, verifies wt_pubkey's \n signature on wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt and updates niso_0_event_block_height with the new value. It checks withdrawal_id to match what was sent, the event_block_heights to be in the appropriate range, and ordered_peer_tx_approvals to contain exactly one approval per active setup peer in peer_ids_collection order. It computes approved_withdrawal_id from withdrawal_id and ordered_peer_tx_approvals. It then generates \n duress_check_space as one randomly sorted list of integers from 1 to 193, including all elements of 1..193, adds a nonce to it and encrypts it. Then Boomlet sends \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st to Niso.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(wt_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/wt_tx_approval", wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  _peer_i_tx_approval := peer_i_tx_approval_signed_by_boomlet_i.content \n _wt_tx_approval := wt_tx_approval_signed_by_wt.content \n update niso_0_event_block_height with received value.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert _peer_i_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert  _wt_tx_approval.withdrawal_id == withdrawal_id.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_approval", ordered_peer_tx_approvals[i]) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
