hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from ST and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 57
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage7 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Niso. Boomlet rejects no outstanding duress check, wrong phase, duplicate response, \n wrong nonce, wrong count, duplicate indices, or out-of-range indices. If valid, Boomlet resolves the returned original-list indices against \n the single list in duress_check_space assigning the resulting integers to duress_signal. \n If the duress_signal is composed of the same set of numbers as the \n duress_consent_set, duress_placeholder_plaintext will be assigned all-zero 32-byte padding otherwise it will be doxing_key_for_sar. \n duress_placeholder_plaintext is updated; the next ping re-encrypts the current plaintext after this optional check.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_signal_index_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_response"), envelope: duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert outstanding duress check exists for current phase \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.nonce == duress_check_nonce \n Assert count(duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices) == 5 \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are distinct \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are in range [1..193]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  consume outstanding duress check \n duress_signal := duress_check_space.space[duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices] \n doxing_key_for_sar := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes) \n duress_placeholder_plaintext := Evaluate(duress_signal, duress_consent_set, doxing_key_for_sar) [either all-zero 32-byte padding or doxing_key_for_sar]
end group
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Regardless of whether a new duress procedure ran, Boomlet freshly encrypts duress_placeholder_plaintext with sar_pubkey to get duress_placeholder. It then checks to see \n if the conditions for incrementing counter are met namely if the local chain view has advanced and prev_ping.last_seen_block is within the accepted boundary. \n If for any of the peer_i_ids not appeared in reached_boomlets_collection, prev_ping_i contains 1-valued reached_mystery_flag, Boomlet assigns \n prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i to reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id]. If Boomlet's own counter has reached its mystery it updates \n reached_mystery_flag value to 1. It then updates the last_seen_block by taking the minimum of the current niso_0_event_block_height and \n previous_last_seen_block + JUMP_IN_BLOCKS_IF_LAST_SEEN_BLOCK_LAGS_BEHIND_NISO_EVENT_BLOCK_HEIGHT_IN_BOOMLET. Boomlet then regenerates ping \n with incremented ping_seq_num, signs it with boomlet_0_identity_privkey, pads it with duress_placeholder, resigns it, encrypts it with wt_pubkey and sends the resulting \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt to Niso.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_placeholder := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", sar_pubkey, "sar", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: sar_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder", approved_withdrawal_id), content: duress_placeholder_plaintext)
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  <b>Counter Increment \n if niso_0_event_block_height > last_seen_block && prev_ping_i.last_seen_block >= (niso_0_event_block_height - TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PING_BY_OTHER_PEERS_TO_REVIEWING_THE_PING_IN_PEER_BOOMLET) && prev_ping_i.last_seen_block <= niso_0_event_block_height : \n previous_last_seen_block := last_seen_block \n counter += 1
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  if reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] == Null and prev_ping_i.reached_mystery_flag==1: \n reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] := prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  if counter >= mystery: \n reached_mystery_flag := 1
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  <b>last_seen_block update after counter increment \n last_seen_block := min(niso_0_event_block_height, (previous_last_seen_block + JUMP_IN_BLOCKS_IF_LAST_SEEN_BLOCK_LAGS_BEHIND_NISO_EVENT_BLOCK_HEIGHT_IN_BOOMLET))
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  _peer_0_ping := Ping{\n approved_withdrawal_id: approved_withdrawal_id, \n last_seen_block: last_seen_block \n ping_seq_num: (ping_seq_num += 1) \n reached_mystery_flag: reached_mystery_flag}\n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", _peer_0_ping) \n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded := PaddedMessage{\n content: _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0, \n padding: duress_placeholder \n} \n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping_envelope", _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded) \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", wt_pubkey, "wt", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: wt_pubkey), context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_ping", approved_withdrawal_id), content: _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0)
end

' Step 58
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage7 \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt from Boomlet and forwards it to WT.

' Step 59
Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage4 \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt
autonumber 59 "<b>[00]"

' Step 59 - b
Peers o-> WT:  peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt from Niso and jumps back to the beginning \n of the PING_PONG_LOOP. if the loop breaks WT sends its reached_pings_collection to all Peers.
end
group Transaction Finalization and Relay

' Step 60
WT o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage4 \n reached_pings_collection
autonumber 60 "<b>[00]"

' Step 60 - b
WT o-> Peers:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage4 \n reached_pings_collection
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives reached_pings_collection from WT. It verifies that the collection contains exactly one current reached ping from every active peer, in active setup peer order, with valid signatures, \n expected approved_withdrawal_id, current ping sequence, fresh last_seen_block, and reached_mystery_flag set. Only after those checks does Niso hydrate the PSBT without changing the transaction semantics or tx_id, then sends reached_pings_collection and hydrated_psbt to Boomlet.
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert count(reached_pings_collection) == count(peer_ids_collection)
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection contains exactly one peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i for each peer_ids_collection[i] [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  peer_i_reached_ping := peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.ping_seq_num >= latest_seen_ping_seq_num_for_peer_i [0 <= i <= 4] \n Assert peer_i_reached_ping.last_seen_block is fresh for current block view [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.reached_mystery_flag == 1 [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection has no missing peers and no duplicate signers
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  hydrated_psbt := hydrate_psbt(psbt)
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert hydrated_psbt.derive_tx_id() == tx_id

' Step 61
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage8 \n reached_pings_collection \n hydrated_psbt
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {reached_pings_collection, hydrated_psbt} from Niso. Boomlet independently verifies that every active peer has exactly one current reached ping for approved_withdrawal_id, \n with current ping sequence, fresh last_seen_block, and reached_mystery_flag set. It then verifies the hydrated PSBT preserves the committed tx_id and remains spendable by the Boomerang descriptor before entering signing.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert count(reached_pings_collection) == count(peer_ids_collection)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection contains exactly one peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i for each peer_ids_collection[i] [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  peer_i_reached_ping := peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.ping_seq_num >= latest_seen_ping_seq_num_for_peer_i [0 <= i <= 4] \n Assert peer_i_reached_ping.last_seen_block is fresh for current block view [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.reached_mystery_flag == 1 [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection has no missing peers and no duplicate signers
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert hydrated_psbt.derive_tx_id() == tx_id.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert hydrate_psbt(hydrated_psbt) != Null
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert psbt_inputs_match_boomerang_descriptor(hydrated_psbt, boomerang_descriptor) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  psbt := hydrated_psbt.

' Step 62
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage8 \n magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush: Niso receives {magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign"} from Boomlet and proceeds to inform User to connect Boomlet to Iso.

' Step 63
Niso o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalNisoOutput1 \n magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign_received_connect_boomlet_to_iso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign_received_connect_boomlet_to_iso"} from Niso and proceeds to connect Boomlet to Iso and input \n network, mnemonic and passphrase to Iso.

' Step 64
User o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalIsoInput1 \n network \n mnemonic \n passphrase
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {network, mnemonic, passphrase} from User, reconstructs the normal private key and normal public key, and proceeds to inform Boomlet that they can start the MuSig2 protocol for tx_ins \n contained in the psbt.
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  master_xpriv_0 := derive_master_xpriv(mnemonic, passphrase) \n purpose_root_xpriv_0 := derive_hardened_child(master_xpriv_0, 52102) \n normal_privkey_0 := purpose_root_xpriv_0 \n normal_pubkey_0 := derive_public_key(normal_privkey_0)

' Step 65
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalIsoBoomletMessage1 \n magic: "withdrawal_initialized_start_signing"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "withdrawal_initialized_start_signing"} from Iso and proceeds to share with it the information necessary for \n signing i.e. psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, alongside his own public nonce named pubnonce_boom.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  pubnonce_boom := musig2_generate_pubnonce(psbt, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share) \n signing_package := {psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, pubnonce_boom}

' Step 66
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletIsoMessage1 \n psbt \n boomerang_descriptor \n boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share \n pubnonce_boom
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, pubnonce_boom} from Boomlet. Iso then generates its own public \n nonce and sends this pubnonce_normal alongside his partialsignature (partialsig_normal) to Boomlet.
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  boom_pubkey_0 := derive_musig2_public_key(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, normal_pubkey_0) \n pubnonce_normal := musig2_generate_pubnonce(psbt, normal_privkey_0) \n partialsig_normal := musig2_partial_sign(normal_privkey_0, psbt, boomerang_descriptor, pubnonce_normal, pubnonce_boom, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share)
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert psbt_is_internally_consistent(psbt) == True
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert psbt_inputs_match_boomerang_descriptor(psbt, boomerang_descriptor) == True
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert boom_pubkey_0 == descriptor_pubkey_for_peer(boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey)

' Step 67
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalIsoBoomletMessage2 \n pubnonce_normal \n partialsig_normal
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {pubnonce_normal, partialsig_normal} from Iso, proceeds to produce its own partial signature and shares it with Iso. \n Boomlet saves signed psbt on its own memory.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert musig2_verify_partial(normal_pubkey_0, partialsig_normal, psbt, pubnonce_normal, pubnonce_boom) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  partialsig_boom := musig2_partial_sign(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share, psbt, boomerang_descriptor, pubnonce_boom, pubnonce_normal, normal_pubkey_0) \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0 := musig2_finalize_psbt(psbt, partialsig_normal, partialsig_boom) \n erase MuSig2 nonce material

' Step 68
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletIsoMessage2 \n partialsig_boom
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives partialsig_boom from Boomlet. Iso also keeps signed psbt but informs User that he can connect Boomlet to Niso.
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert musig2_verify_partial(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, partialsig_boom, psbt, pubnonce_boom, pubnonce_normal) == True
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  psbt_signed_by_peer_0 := musig2_finalize_psbt(psbt, partialsig_normal, partialsig_boom) \n erase MuSig2 nonce material

' Step 69
Iso o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalIsoOutput1 \n magic: "withdrawal_psbt_signature_created_connect_boomlet_to_niso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "withdrawal_psbt_signature_created_connect_boomlet_to_niso"} from Iso and proceeds to connect Boomlet to Niso.

' Step 70
User o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalNisoInput2 \n magic: "withdrawal_peer_is_informed_that_boomlet_should_be_connected_to_niso"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {magic: "withdrawal_peer_is_informed_that_boomlet_should_be_connected_to_niso"} from User and proceeds to ask Boomlet for \n the signed psbt.

' Step 71
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage9 \n magic: "withdrawal_signing_finished_export_signed_psbt"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "withdrawal_signing_finished_export_signed_psbt"} from Niso and proceeds to respond to Niso with psbt_signed_by_peer_0. \n It also clears its memory of other withdrawal-specific information, including the ceremony mystery.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  withdrawal_clear() [reset memory back to pre-withdrawal except psbt_signed_by_peer_0]

' Step 72
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage9 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives psbt_signed_by_peer_0 from Boomlet and forwards it to WT.

' Step 73
Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage5 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0
autonumber 73 "<b>[00]"

' Step 73 - b
Peers o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage5 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_i [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives psbt_signed_by_peer_0 from Niso and psbt_signed_by_peer_i [1 <= i <= 4] from Peers. WT verifies that every signed PSBT fragment belongs to the approved withdrawal transaction, \n aggregates the signed PSBTs, verifies the final transaction tx_id, and relays the resulting tx_signed_by_peers to the network.
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert psbt_signed_by_peer_i.derive_tx_id() == tx_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert psbt_signed_by_peer_i belongs to approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Lavender:  tx_signed_by_peers := aggregate_psbt(psbt_signed_by_peer_i) [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert tx_signed_by_peers.derive_tx_id() == tx_id
hnote over WT #Lavender:  relay_tx(tx_signed_by_peers, network)
end
@endpuml
